# Salted digests of the words this repository must never contain.
#
# There is no plaintext here on purpose. A rule that spells out what it
# forbids publishes the string it exists to suppress, and a rule written
# to exempt its own file leaves the one file nobody scans as the one file
# that names them. Regenerate with scripts/gen-forbidden-tokens.py from
# the private word list; reuse --salt to keep the diff to one line.
#
# Readers lowercase each line and slide a window of every declared
# length across it, looking up sha256(salt + window). That reproduces a
# case-insensitive substring search exactly, so a word glued inside a
# longer identifier is still caught. The lengths must be declared for
# the window to exist; leaking a word length is far less than the word.
#
# This is obscurity, not secrecy: the candidate space is small
# enough to brute-force -- and it is sized to the actual threat: a
# careless paste, a search engine, and a casual reader.
